th1 → rh1 (246666 arrives). Cost $1.4004\n4. `q_7` rh1: swap 246666 WBTC → ≈0.0492332 ETH. Cost $0.36\n5. `q_6` Bridge 0.001 ETH from eth1 → arb1 for gas (≈0.000833 ETH arrives). Cost $1.40\n6. `q_3` Bridge 247500 WBTC from eth1 → arb1 (246666 arrives). Cost $1.4004\n7. `q_8` arb1: swap 246666 WBTC → ≈147.6996 USDC. Cost $0.36\n\n**Total cost: $10.2208.** Your policy cap is $15.00, so this fits.\n\n- **Why the gas bridges:** rh1 and arb1 have 0 ETH, so they can't pay for their own swaps. Bridges smaller than 0.001 ETH were rejected because the fee would eat the whole amount. After the route, both wallets keep enough ETH for at least one more transaction.\n- **Option I didn't pick:** swapping to USDC on Ethereum and then bridging the USDC to Arbitrum would cost about $13.76 and give less USDC (145.5 vs 147.7). Arbitrum would still need ETH sent over for gas.\n- **Left on eth1:** about 0.0465 ETH after gas.\n- **Expiry:** quotes expire after 300 s, and the 4 bridges take about 60 s each. If a quote expires during the run, I'll get a new one before submitting that leg.\n\nReply **approve** to run it, set a lower cost cap, or reject."}]},{"role":"user","sequence":22,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, go ahead with that plan."}]},{"role":"assistant","sequence":23,"content":[{"type":"toolCall","name":"mcp__ai_sdk_harness_tools_execute_leg","arguments":{"quote_id":"q_1","approval_id":"appr_9"},"id":"toolu_01CRme3BCtUm2nxE1ZL7LoJZ"}]},{"role":"tool","sequence":24,"content":[{"type":"toolResult","text":"{\"tx_id\":\"tx_10\"}","toolCallId":"toolu_01CRme3BCtUm2nxE1ZL7LoJZ","toolName":"mcp__ai_sdk_harness_tools_execute_leg","isError":false}]},{"role":"assistant","sequence":25,"content":[{"type":"toolCall","name":"mcp__ai_sdk_harness_tools_tx_status","arguments":{"tx_id":"tx_10"},"id":"toolu_01M8jGMTtZ6xrLVxQSk8HMcD"}]},{"role":"tool","sequence":26,"content":[{"type":"toolResult","text":"{\"status\":\"confirmed\"}","toolCallId":"toolu_01M8jGMTtZ6xrLVxQSk8HMcD","toolName":"mc